 <umutcagand@protonmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:54:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] libcomparetf2: Add the remaining long double comparisons

Android 17 libc no longer exports these compiler-rt helpers; Samsung's
libOpenCv.camera.samsung imports __eqtf2, __netf2, __letf2, __gttf2
and __unordtf2 next to __lttf2. __getf2 is added for completeness.
The shim assumes a 128-bit IEEE long double, so build it for arm64 only.

Assisted-by: LLM
Change-Id: I3aa83783a15650f7b7aed0a3cadfb5bb7dff0384
---
 Android.bp                 |  7 +++++++
 libcomparetf2/comparetf2.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index 0c86695..6db6e9b 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -692,6 +692,13 @@ cc_library_shared {
     srcs: ["libcomparetf2/comparetf2.c"],
     compile_multilib: "64",
     vendor: true,
+    // Assumes 128-bit IEEE long double (arm64 only)
+    enabled: false,
+    arch: {
+        arm64: {
+            enabled: true,
+        },
+    },
 }
 
 cc_prebuilt_library_shared {
diff --git a/libcomparetf2/comparetf2.c b/libcomparetf2/comparetf2.c
index e725133..fa04b20 100644
--- a/libcomparetf2/comparetf2.c
+++ b/libcomparetf2/comparetf2.c
@@ -69,3 +69,19 @@ enum LE_RESULT __lttf2(fp_t a, fp_t b) {
       return LE_GREATER;
   }
 }
+
+enum LE_RESULT __letf2(fp_t a, fp_t b) __attribute__((alias("__lttf2")));
+enum LE_RESULT __eqtf2(fp_t a, fp_t b) __attribute__((alias("__lttf2")));
+enum LE_RESULT __netf2(fp_t a, fp_t b) __attribute__((alias("__lttf2")));
+
+int __unordtf2(fp_t a, fp_t b) {
+  return (toRep(a) & absMask) > infRep || (toRep(b) & absMask) > infRep;
+}
+
+int __gttf2(fp_t a, fp_t b) {
+  if (__unordtf2(a, b))
+    return -1;
+  return __lttf2(a, b);
+}
+
+int __getf2(fp_t a, fp_t b) __attribute__((alias("__gttf2")));
